From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Melser <anton.melser@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 12:42:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] build-emscripten: add the Emscripten port and its build
 targets

Add an "emscripten" port and the build hooks the PGlite build scripts
(build-pglite.sh and pglite/ in the overlay) rely on:

- src/template/emscripten, src/include/port/emscripten.h and
  src/makefiles/Makefile.emscripten define the port: unnamed POSIX
  semaphores, poll-based waits, fdatasync as the default WAL sync
  method, no inlining, unversioned shared libraries, and the install
  directories for extension import lists.
- src/backend/Makefile links the backend as pglite (with
  POSTGRES_PGLITE_FLAGS), installs pglite.wasm/.js/.data, and computes
  exported_functions.txt: every built extension's imports plus
  pglite/static/included.pglite.exports, minus the symbols the linked
  libraries provide.
- src/makefiles/pgxs.mk and src/pl/plpgsql/src/Makefile write each
  extension's undefined symbols to an .imports list, the input to that
  export list; src/Makefile.shlib links shared libraries with the
  compiler and without versioned names.
- The initdb, pg_config, pg_ctl and pg_dump Makefiles install their
  .wasm outputs; pg_config and pg_ctl are wrapped by
  pglite/scripts/run_pg_cmd.mjs so other tools can run them.
- contrib/Makefile builds pgcrypto when PGLITE_WITH_PGCRYPTO=1 and
  includes the overlay's contrib/dist.mk; src/timezone/Makefile uses the
  host's zic.
- configure puts "(PGlite $PGLITE_VERSION)" into PG_VERSION_STR, so
  version() names the build.
- .gitignore ignores the build outputs.

Derived from electric-sql/postgres-pglite b133782cd759f08b3aeb263b80a963b39c7b7af1 (PostgreSQL 18.3 fork, PostgreSQL License)
